+.. _hookimpl_arg_default:
+
+Hookimpl argument defaults
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+A *hookimpl* can also declare a default value for an argument. This allows a
+plugin to use a new argument while still supporting older versions of the
+host program, whose *hookspec* does not have the argument yet.
+
+The value a *hookimpl* receives for such an argument is, in order of
+precedence:
+
+1. the value passed by the hook call,
+2. the default value declared by the *hookspec*,
+3. the default value declared by the *hookimpl* itself.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @hookspec
+    def myhook(config, args, new_arg="spec default"):
+        pass
+
+
+    @hookimpl
+    def myhook(args, new_arg="impl default", newer_arg="impl default"):
+        print(new_arg, newer_arg)
+
+
+    # Prints "spec default impl default".
+    pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args)
+    # Prints "get this impl default".
+    pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args, new_arg="get this")
+
+This applies to plain *hookimpls* as well as to :ref:`wrappers <hookwrappers>`
+and :ref:`old-style hook wrappers <old_style_hookwrappers>`.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 1.7
+    Previously, the default value declared by a *hookimpl* was always used,
+    even if the hook call passed a value for the argument.
 
 
